"[CSS] Run the marking barrier when switching a CSSSelector to RareData"
(crbugs 574409610 and 577610454, not public; no CVE listed yet): switching a
CSSSelector to its rare data (or to a selector list) placement-constructed a
Member, which skips Oilpan's marking write barrier. The parser's :host:has()
fix-up does this on a selector that may already have been traced, so the
garbage collector could miss the new object and free it while still in use.
The Member is now constructed empty and assigned, so the barrier runs.
chromium/src main commit c3af608c93903126b2690260c2a3c9879c47d234, merged on
2026-11-03 to 157 (01ed020f9735f1103aacecf764c5ab12aaed0e86, after the
157.0.8103.41 tag). This is the 157 merge, without its test. Drop it once a
157 tag has it.

